// ============================================================================
// Hunt: Compromised mailbox used as a phishing cannon (anomalous outbound
// mail volume) + suspicious inbox forwarding rules
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1078 (Valid Accounts), T1534 (Internal Spearphishing)
// Data: Microsoft Defender - EmailEvents, OfficeActivity
// Write-up: https://amitvijayan.com/journal/articles/daily-cyber-threat-brief-october-6-2026.html
// Logic: on Sep 30, 2026 an attacker used a compromised Nikkei Microsoft 365
// account to send ~9,000 phishing emails to journalists and sources. The
// initial access vector was not disclosed and no IoCs were published, so this
// is a behavioral hunt: (1) per-sender outbound mail volume spikes in
// EmailEvents, and (2) new/changed inbox rules that forward or redirect mail
// in OfficeActivity - the classic "keep the access after the password reset"
// move. The separate Google Workspace intrusion (Jul-Aug 2026, surfaced only
// via a Google notification) is a reminder this pattern applies to any cloud
// mail tenant, not just M365.
// ============================================================================

// -- Variant 1: senders with a sudden burst of outbound mail
// A single user sending thousands of messages in an hour is the Nikkei tell.
EmailEvents
| where TimeGenerated > ago(7d)
| summarize SentCount = count(),
            UniqueRecipients = dcount(RecipientEmailAddress),
            SampleSubjects = make_set(Subject, 10)
    by SenderFromAddress, SenderIPv4, bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)
| where SentCount >= 200 or UniqueRecipients >= 100
| order by SentCount desc

// -- Variant 2: inbox rules created or changed to forward/redirect mail
// Attackers on a mailbox add forwarding rules so replies and sensitive mail
// keep flowing to them even after the password is changed.
OfficeActivity
| where TimeGenerated > ago(30d)
| where Operation in~ ("New-InboxRule", "Set-InboxRule", "UpdateInboxRule")
| where Parameters has "ForwardTo"
    or Parameters has "ForwardAsAttachmentTo"
    or Parameters has "RedirectTo"
| project TimeGenerated, Operation, UserId, ClientIP, Parameters
| order by TimeGenerated desc
